{# RFC §5.B B5-θ codec test-vector sidecar. Each row pins one wire
   `hex` byte sequence to a flat `<sce:decoded>` field tree; the
   emitted `#[test]` builds the codec struct, asserts encode → bytes
   parity, then decodes the same bytes back and asserts every field
   matches. Trunk lands on plain (non-variant, non-TLV-chain, non-
   parent-flags, non-repeat, non-present-if) codecs only — those
   shapes reject upstream in `render_codec_test_vector_sidecar` so
   authors get a precise gate error rather than a broken sidecar. #}

